# Private development assets — real files, never committed.
# ../blackbull-assets holds the frozen history of the planning material that
# moved to the tracker.  It is no longer symlinked in: these are working files
# now, and the companion repo is an archive rather than their home.
.claude
# Project-scoped dsh skill discovery root — symlinks into the frozen skills
# archive (../blackbull-assets/frozen/skills), machine-local, never committed.
.dsh
# CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md — create locally: ln -s AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.md
# Convenience link so GitHub-side tooling finds the skills locally — create
# with: ln -s ../.claude/skills .github/skills
# Untracked deliberately: it resolves through .claude above, which is ignored,
# so a committed symlink would arrive dangling in every clone and in CI.
.github/skills

# bench/lib is the bench tools' shared code, not a build artefact (lib/ above).
!bench/lib/
# bench run output — see bench/results/README.md
bench/results/*
!bench/results/README.md
# bench runtime state: cloud session, key, known hosts (bench/cloud/config.sh)
bench/.state/

# bench/httparena — local sandbox mounts (dataset + dev certs).  See
# bench/httparena/README.md for the local smoke-test recipe.
bench/httparena/_local/
# A locally-built wheel that Dockerfile.dev installs from.  Untracked
# so the dev image always builds against fresh source.
bench/httparena/blackbull-*.whl
# peer benchmark harness — work-in-progress automated runner.
# Kept on disk for future development; not committed until the socket-state
# contamination is solved cleanly.
bench/compare/compare.sh
bench/compare/httparena_calibrate.py
bench/compare/bench/results/*
# peer benchmark harness — private development notes
*.private.md

# mutation testing workspace (just mutate)
mutants/
